        "id": 1060959
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-30T16:54:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Based on the above comments why is this ok?\n\nWe should be able to build the resulting merged stub against nothing. I think that prevents the \"depending on systemapi from a publicapi stub\" problem.\n\n\u003e Presumably module_current is not going to be built by combining this and other stubs so what is going to be done instead?\n\nmodule_current we be build from the srcs of all of these modules, but only modules are allowed to build against it, so it avoids the cycle without sacrificing any safety I think.\n\n\u003e Is it because there are already circular dependencies in it?\n\nYeah, there are circular dependencies between the non-updatable part and the modules, so I don\u0027t think we can draw a DAG without module_current or something else like it",
      "parentUuid": "dce95f01_0f51d4b8",
